--- backend/internal/service/chat/skill_scan.go:299 ---
👮 **Wachiman** · 🟠🐛 **Fix · bug: filepath.WalkDir does not follow a symlinked commands folder, so its commands silently disappear (confidence medium)**

The old code used `os.ReadDir(root.dir)`, which follows a symlink at the root. `commandFiles` now calls `filepath.WalkDir(dir, ...)`. WalkDir `Lstat`s the root and does not follow symlinks. If `~/.claude/commands` or `<project>/.claude/commands` is a symlink to a directory (common when it points into a dotfiles repo), the callback gets the symlink as a non-directory entry whose name doesn't end in `.md`. It returns nil, so no commands are listed. The error is swallowed (`_ =`) and nothing is logged, so the `/` menu just omits every user command. Skill folders still work because they use `os.Stat`. Resolve the root first, e.g. `if resolved, err := filepath.EvalSymlinks(dir); err == nil { dir = resolved }` before walking. Add a test with a symlinked commands dir. I did not run the code; this follows from the documented `WalkDir` behaviour.

